THPS3 recomp host: third-party code and credits
================================================

This directory holds our own host code, configs and tools. No game data, no ROM bytes and no
recompiled game code are in it (those are generated on your machine from your own dump).

Code adapted from, or structured after, other projects (all GPL-3.0 or compatible):

  Zelda64Recomp (https://github.com/Zelda64Recomp/Zelda64Recomp, GPL-3.0)
    src/rt64_context.cpp   RT64 render context, derived from Zelda64Recomp's ui_renderer / rt64_render_context
                           (as carried in RecompFrontend)
    src/audio.cpp          queue_samples left/right handling
    src/platform.{h,cpp}   the split between Windows, Linux and macOS (window and renderer handle, window
    src/main.cpp           flags, DPI awareness, timeBeginPeriod, WASAPI default, per-user config folders,
                           portable.txt) follows Zelda64Recomp's src/main/main.cpp
    CMakeLists.txt         Windows (clang-cl) and Linux (RT64_SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN) build settings follow Zelda64Recomp's

Libraries the host builds against (fetched by tools/setup_runtime.py at the pinned commits, patched by
patches/*.patch; none of their source is stored here):

  N64ModernRuntime (https://github.com/N64Recomp/N64ModernRuntime) and N64Recomp, MIT
  RT64 (https://github.com/rt64/rt64) with plume, MIT
  SDL2, zlib licence. On Windows the host uses the SDL2 2.26.3 that RT64 bundles.
  Microsoft DirectX Shader Compiler: on Windows, dxcompiler.dll and dxil.dll from Microsoft's DirectXShaderCompiler
  release v1.8.2407 (dxc_2024_07_31.zip, downloaded at build time by tools/setup_runtime.py, SHA-256 pinned) are copied
  next to the executable (they are loaded at run time); RT64's own contrib/dxc is used only as a build tool. Their
  licence texts ship in resources/licenses/, unchanged, from that release: DXC-dxcompiler.txt (the LLVM Release
  License, University of Illinois/NCSA) and DXC-dxil.txt (Microsoft Software License Terms for the DirectX Shader
  Compiler, whose "Distributable Code" section sets the terms for distributing dxil.dll in an application).

In-game settings menu (THPS_MENU, on by default; src/ui/ and ui/ in the shared host):
  Zelda64Recomp (https://github.com/Zelda64Recomp/Zelda64Recomp, GPL-3.0, commit b65c482)
    src/ui/ui_renderer.{h,cpp}   RmlUi on RT64, from src/ui/ui_renderer.cpp (RT64:: -> plume:: namespace changes only)
    ui/shaders/Interface{VS,PS}.hlsl  its two RmlUi shaders, unchanged
    src/ui/ui_host.cpp           structure after src/ui/ui_state.cpp (event queue, draw hook, controller key repeat)
    ui/menu/recomp.rcss, rml.rcss  its menu styles (compiled from its SCSS); changed: the font family (chiaro -> LatoLatin), colour alpha 0..1 -> 0..255
    ui/menu/settings.rml         the tab/option markup follows its assets/config_menu*.rml
    ui/menu/icons/X.svg          its close icon
  Libraries built into the menu (fetched at pinned commits by tools/setup_runtime.py, none stored here): RmlUi 6.0 (MIT),
    lunasvg (MIT), FreeType 2.13.3 (FreeType License / GPL-2.0; we use the FTL: portions of this software are copyright
    The FreeType Project, www.freetype.org. All rights reserved.).
  Fonts shipped with a THPS_MENU build (SIL Open Font License 1.1, fetched and SHA-256 checked, not stored in git; the licence text is
    ui/FONTS-LICENSE.txt, shipped as resources/ui/fonts/LICENSE.txt): Lato (Latin subset, (c) 2011-2015 tyPoland Lukasz Dziedzic),
    Noto Emoji ((c) Google), PromptFont (Yukari "Shinmera" Hafner; based on Xolonium by Severin Meyer).
  NOT used: Zelda64Recomp's ChiaroNormal/ChiaroBold fonts (Fontworks Japan, commercial) and its Majora's Mask artwork.

Optional launcher build (THPS3_WITH_RECOMPFRONTEND, local use only): RecompFrontend, which has no
licence yet (N64Recomp/RecompFrontend issue #44).
